    <string name="settings_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="settings_privacy_body">Budget Companion talks to one place only: the Nextcloud server you sign in to. It never contacts Otherworld Dev or anyone else, and it has no analytics, crash reporting, advertising or tracking.\n\nYour app password is kept in Android\'s encrypted storage on the phone, and signing out revokes it on your server.\n\nReceipt photos are sent to your server with the transaction you save, and each photo is deleted from the phone once its transaction has been saved. Reading a receipt happens on your server, using whichever method its administrator has set up.\n\nSo the app works without a signal, it keeps a copy of your accounts, categories, budgets, bills and recent transactions on the phone. Signing out deletes all of it, and none of it goes into Android\'s cloud backup.\n\nThe same policy is published at budget.otherworld.dev/privacy.html.</string>

